descriptionByLocale.en:
Active in Western Switzerland, we help our customers to carry out their projects by providing comprehensive, efficient and sustainable energy solutions, whether in the production and distribution of electricity and heat, electrical installations, home automation, soft mobility, air conditioning or water treatment. As an exemplary employer, we support the development of the skills of our 2450 employees, including 245 apprentices, and the reconciliation between private and professional life. The Finance and Information Technology Directorate provides its expertise in the financial management of the company, procurement and wealth as well as IT services. Mission:
• Ensure the quality, reliability and governance of procurement data to provide a sound basis for strategic decisions;
• Design and develop dashboards, performance indicators and analyses (depends, savings, forecasts) to accompany the management of purchases;
• Identify opportunities for continuous improvement and automate processes through digital solutions (Power Automation, RPA, ERP D365);
• Ensure the role of Key User of the ERP Procurement module by providing level 2 support and participating in tool evolutions and testing phases;
• Work closely with the Purchasing, IT, Finance and Trade teams to harmonize data, coordinate needs and ensure consistency of processes across the Group;
• Ensure consistency and updating of the procurement documentation library, and prepare and coordinate internal and external audits by ensuring compliance, traceability and availability of information. Profile:
• Bachelor's degree in Management Information Technology, Business Economics or equivalent training;
• Experience in a Procurement environment and/or in creating dashboards and reporting tools, an asset;
• Excellent mastery of Power BI, Advanced Excel (Power Query), SQL, Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations and Microsoft Office suite;
• Analytic spirit, rigour, autonomy, sense of organization and ease of collaboration with various interlocutors. What we offer:
• An evolving environment conducive to work-life balance.
• Social benefits of a modern enterprise, fair treatment, opportunities for professional development.
• A strong spirit of cohesion and a team proud to collaborate: "Together for tomorrow's energy" Need more information? Contact Valentin Dayer, Head of Purchasing at 026 352 54 46 Interested? We look forward to receiving your full application by clicking on the "Post" button below. Human resources Brice Muller Apply » Search for similar jobs: Unsere offene Stellen, Vacancy
